WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.602
 All right, guys,
congratulations.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.471
It is now down to the two
of you to battle it out,

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.873
figure out who's going home
with the title of Forged in Fire

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.074
champion and a
check for $10,000.

00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:10.610
In round three, we're
going to be sending

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.911
you guys back to
your home forges

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.213
to work on this
blade for four days.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.017
The blade we're going to
have you guys build is this.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:25.692
The William Wallace sword.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.259
Big'un right?

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:29.462
NARRATOR: Armed with his
gigantic, two-handed claymore,

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.130
William Wallace was
known for leading

00:00:31.196 --> 00:00:32.999
the Scottish rebellion
against the English

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.201
during the late 12th century.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.837
Measuring in at a staggering
5 foot 4 inches tall,

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.039
the blade weighed
less than 6 pounds,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.008
making it both lightweight
and long enough

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.810
to deliver deadly blows
against the enemy on horseback

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.378
or on foot.

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:48.948
Wallace led his troops to
victory with his namesake sword

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:51.116
during the famous Battle
of Stirling Bridge.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.553
Memorialized as a
Scottish hero, Wallace

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.890
can be seen wielding his iconic
sword in the 1995 blockbuster,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.258
"Braveheart."

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.027
 This is the largest
sword we've ever

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:02.495
asked any bladesmiths to make.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:06.199
 One look at that beautiful
sword, and I think, nope.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.034
[laughs]

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.336
 You've got to make your
blades within these parameters.

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:12.338
The blade length
needs to be between 51

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:15.742
and 53 inches with a blade
width no less than 2 inches.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.744
You guys need to have a
guard with upswept quillians,

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.947
langei, and two side rings.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.915
Need to include a
two-handed handle,

00:01:22.981 --> 00:01:24.517
and top it off with a pommel.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.019
The best of luck to
both of you guys.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:30.123
We'll see you back in
the forge in four days.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.493
[music playing]

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:34.660
 Here we are.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:35.561
Round three.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.729
Championship round.

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:37.997
Let's start this bad boy out.

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:41.033
And a big challenge
making a big sword.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.935
I've made a few swords,
but never have I

00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:45.104
made anything of this caliber.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.072
That's a 32 inch blade.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:50.376
I need 20 more inches.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.846
The key to victory with a
weapon this size is performance,

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.147
and it's all about
that heat treat.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:56.682
That is the most critical part.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.550
Yeah.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.685
Oh, that looks great.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.420
I like it, I like it, I like it.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.254
[sizzling]

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.788
Just a little fire.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.790
Just a little fire.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.159
Whoo!

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.794
It seems to have taken great.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:12.097
I am ecstatic.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:14.000
That went wonderfully.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.401
Oh, man, I'm feeling great.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.337
This sword is enormous,
and it is light.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.105
I want to wield this thing.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.774
There's not a lot of
reasons to walk around town

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.310
with a chainmail shirt,
unless you have a William

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:27.046
Wallace sword, then
of course, you should

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.214
have a chainmail shirt on.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:32.952
That's pretty nice.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.620
That cut really well.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.290
 I'm back in Bloomsburg,
Pennsylvania, my home forge.

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:40.092
I got to make a
William Wallace sword.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.228
It's a beastly sword.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.263
Today, I would like to
get the blade drawn out

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:46.365
to rough parameters, hopefully.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.466
I can't screw this up.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:50.636
I only have one piece of this.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:53.105
So now that I've got my
rough shape formed in,

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:54.973
I get the angle grinder
that way I can look

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.676
for [inaudible] and cracks.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:58.377
Looks good.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.879
I don't see the cracks.

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:02.681
I have to get this quench done.

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.150
Here we go.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.551
I'm just worried about
something going wrong with this

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.787
because it takes way too
much time to make this,

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.224
and I don't have enough
time to do another one.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.992
Get in there.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:13.893
Come on, you [bleep].

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.562
[sizzling]

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.433
[grinding]

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.204
Got a little bit of a warp
in it, but it's not bad.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:26.973
I'm pretty happy with it.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:29.509
It's time to start putting
all the pieces of this sword

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:30.543
together.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.344
I slipped the guard
down on my sword.

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:35.114
And the challenge is just making
sure everything fits tight

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:37.049
and there's no wiggling,
there's no moving.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.417
Because if they hit
it off something

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.753
and if something loosens
up, I could go home.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.289
I'm really happy with
the way it looks.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.224
Big sword for a big guy.

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:46.359
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.494
Welcome to the kill test.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.129
To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:03:50.195 --> 00:03:52.498
your iconic William
Wallace swords will do,

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.134
I will take your sword
and deliver lethal blows

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:57.370
on this wild boar carcass.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.237
James, you're up first.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.004
You ready for this?

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.072
 Yes, I am.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.507
 All right, let's do it.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:04.477
 Those hogs can take out
a weapon pretty easily.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.679
It could wrap around the
side of the hog instead

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.947
of cutting into the hog.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.082
And all that momentum could
go into bending the blade

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.018
rather than slicing
into the pig,

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:14.086
and that makes me very nervous.

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:17.055
 That is massive.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:20.727
[music playing]

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.035
 Whoa.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.511
[thud]

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:40.412
 All right, James.

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:41.747
Let's talk about
your blade here.

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:43.582
Pocket knife, it is not.

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:46.185
But this long blade actually
has a nice weight to it.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.253
It's wieldable with two hands.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:51.157
Grabbing on to your handle
here, I get a good grip.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.459
Your edge is razor sharp.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:56.829
It easily punctures and
has a nice draw cut to it.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:05:00.232
Now cutting the carcass, as
you can see, it cut it in half.

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:03.669
And more importantly,
sir, it'll kill.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.536
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:05.538
 All right, Lyle.
Your turn.

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:06.606
So you ready?
- Yes, sir.

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:07.440
 Let's do it.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.845
 My stomach is
just in not knots.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.547
I'm nervous about my quench.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.048
And, you know, I'm just--

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:19.218
I didn't know if I did it right,
but I'm going to find out.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:22.288
I'm ready for it to be over.

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.992
[music playing]

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:49.749
 All right, let's
talk about your William

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:50.449
Wallace sword here.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.516
It's a lighter sword.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.152
It's about a half
a pound lighter.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:55.387
Your edge is sharp.

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.456
Now it cut very deep
on this pig carcass.

00:05:57.522 --> 00:06:00.359
It didn't cut it in
half, but it did cut.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.861
Overall sir, your
sword, it will kill.

00:06:02.961 --> 00:06:03.763
 Thank you.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.701
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:12.071
It's time for the strength
test, our battering ram chop.

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:15.041
Now why would you attack a
battering ram with a sword?

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:16.075
I don't know.

00:06:16.141 --> 00:06:17.309
But we're going to do it anyway.

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:18.577
Now remember, this
test is not about what

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.012
your sword will do
to that battering ram

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.313
but how well they hold up.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:22.214
James, you're up first.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:23.048
You ready?

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:23.882
 Dave, I hate this plan.

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:25.918
[laughter]

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.126
[grunts]

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:39.131
[exhales]

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:40.499
 All right, James.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:43.402
Blade is still true as
it was when we started.

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:44.603
It's comfortable.

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.238
It's strong, and
man, it held up well.

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:47.572
Good job.

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:48.374
 Yeah, I really like
hearing you talk about it.

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:49.174
That's great.

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:50.242
[laughter]

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:51.243
 All right, Lyle.

00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:52.077
Your turn.

00:06:52.177 --> 00:06:52.845
Ready?

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:53.546
 I guess.

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:54.414
I guess.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:04.123
[grunts]

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:08.094
[rock music]

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.237
 All right, Lyle.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:22.007
First off, remarkable job making
a weapon this big, this light,

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.476
and hold up that well.

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:24.910
That's impressive.

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:30.349
But the issue is we've got
some loosening going on.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:31.950
Other than that,
you did a great job.

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:32.718
 Thank you.

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.424
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.859
This is the sharpness test,
the foam pillar slice.

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:43.595
Now unlike the strength test,
this is all about how sharp

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:45.731
your weapons are and what
they do to these foam pillars

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.232
that are wrapped in leather.

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.434
James, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:49.735
 Yeah, man.
Let's go.

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:50.570
 Let's do it.

00:07:59.077 --> 00:08:02.682
[rock music]

00:08:09.454 --> 00:08:10.890
All right, James.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.927
The edge of your sword is
like cutting through butter.

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.228
It's a nice, clean cut.

00:08:16.328 --> 00:08:17.630
Cuts all the way through.

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:22.033
Overall sir, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.969
 Thank you.

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:23.602
 All right, Lyle.

00:08:23.702 --> 00:08:25.003
You're turn, sir.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:25.738
You ready?

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:26.304
 Yes, sir.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:27.305
Let's do this.

00:08:27.372 --> 00:08:30.910
[rock music]

00:08:37.349 --> 00:08:38.383
 All right, Lyle.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.819
Let's talk about
your sword here.

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:42.621
First off, the guard
is still a little bit

00:08:42.687 --> 00:08:44.023
loose from the strength test.

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:47.192
But when it comes to the
cuts, it is a sharp edge

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:48.093
that you have here.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.294
It did cut the leather.

00:08:49.361 --> 00:08:50.629
It just didn't cut through.

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:53.432
It's a lighter blade,
thinner edge over here.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:56.034
But it does cut.

00:08:56.101 --> 00:08:58.203
 Thank you.

00:08:58.303 --> 00:08:59.805
 All right, gentlemen.

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:02.508
You guys both brought us back
giant William Wallace swords

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:04.142
that exceeded our expectations.

00:09:04.209 --> 00:09:06.678
They're the largest swords
ever built in this competition,

00:09:06.745 --> 00:09:08.680
so we want to commend
you guys both for that.

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:11.416
But there can only be one
champion in this competition.

00:09:11.483 --> 00:09:13.219
And today's Forged
in Fire champion is--

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:17.456
James.

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:18.223
Congratulations.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.758
 Thank you.

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:20.960
 Lyle, unfortunately you just
didn't make the cut today.

00:09:21.026 --> 00:09:22.761
And Dave Baker's
going to tell you why.

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:25.931
 Lyle, you made us an amazing
sword that performed very well.

00:09:26.031 --> 00:09:28.000
But the guard loosened
up in the strength test,

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:30.236
and it just didn't cut as
well in the sharpness test.

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:31.403
And that's why we're
letting you go.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.704
 I understand.

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:33.839
 Lyle, thank you for
all your hard work.

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:35.207
You produced a
phenomenal weapon,

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:36.542
but unfortunately, I'm
going to have to ask you,

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:37.476
please step off the floor.

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.278
 Thank you.

00:09:39.344 --> 00:09:40.846
I'm a little upset that I lost.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:45.084
But at the same time, I mean,
I got nothing to be sad about.

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:49.021
To be here at the finals, and my
sword actually made it through.

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:52.358
I mean, I can't be
more happy about it.

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:56.528
 James, congratulations.

00:09:56.628 --> 00:09:57.896
You are the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:09:57.997 --> 00:10:00.967
You'll be leaving here
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:01.533
How does it feel?

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.868
 Pretty great.

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:03.702
Yeah, baby!

00:10:03.768 --> 00:10:06.371
I am Forged in Fire champion.

00:10:06.438 --> 00:10:08.140
 Great work.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.908
 Feels a little surreal.

00:10:09.975 --> 00:10:11.744
Like, maybe this isn't real.

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:14.146
I might find out tomorrow that
this didn't really happen.

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:17.683
[music playing]

